Description: vo_gpu: keep the integer-texture divisor out of the printed multiplier
 copy_image() folded 1/(2^bits-1) into img.multiplier and printed it into the
 shader with "%f". For a 16-bit integer plane holding MSB-aligned 10-bit data
 (P010, component_pad > 0) the multiplier is about 1.0039/65535 = 1.53e-5,
 which "%f" prints as 0.000015: the plane comes out 2.1 % dark (1.7 % for
 full-range or RGB 16-bit data). The divisor is now written into the shader
 separately ("... * vec4(texture(...)).r / 65535.0"), and taken from the
 texture's own component depth.
 .
 Affects any setup where vo_gpu samples a 16-bit integer texture: GPUs without
 normalised 16-bit formats, or a hwdec interop that maps integer planes.
 Measured on an Orange Pi 5B (Mali-G610): vo_gpu drew an integer-sampled P010
 frame 2-3 % dark (37 dB against copy-back, max 7 8-bit steps); with this
 change 79.9 dB, max one step, no bias.
 .
 Written with Claude (Anthropic): the LLM found the bug from a same-frame
 picture comparison and wrote the change; the maintainer tested it.
Author: defcom5-rockchip <286489597+defcom5-rockchip@users.noreply.github.com>
Origin: vendor, Pi-Desktop
Forwarded: not-yet
Last-Update: 2026-10-09
---
diff --git a/video/out/gpu/video.c b/video/out/gpu/video.c
index eabf917..2ced328 100644
--- a/video/out/gpu/video.c
+++ b/video/out/gpu/video.c
@@ -1429,13 +1429,17 @@ static void copy_image(struct gl_video *p, unsigned int *offset, struct image im
         dst[i] = dst_fmt[*offset + i];
     }
 
+    // Integer textures are normalised in the shader. The divisor stays out of
+    // the multiplier: folded in, a 16-bit one leaves a value around 1.5e-5,
+    // which "%f" prints as 0.000015, a 2 % error on the whole picture.
+    char norm[32] = "";
     if (img.tex && img.tex->params.format->ctype == RA_CTYPE_UINT) {
-        uint64_t tex_max = 1ull << p->ra_format.component_bits;
-        img.multiplier *= 1.0 / (tex_max - 1);
+        uint64_t tex_max = 1ull << img.tex->params.format->component_depth[0];
+        snprintf(norm, sizeof(norm), " / %.1f", (double)(tex_max - 1));
     }
 
-    GLSLF("color.%s = %f * vec4(texture(texture%d, texcoord%d)).%s;\n",
-          dst, img.multiplier, id, id, src);
+    GLSLF("color.%s = %f * vec4(texture(texture%d, texcoord%d)).%s%s;\n",
+          dst, img.multiplier, id, id, src, norm);
 
     *offset += count;
 }
